This is a '''list of airports in [[Balboa]]''', a country comprising five provinces on the [[Balboa Isthmus|isthmus]] connecting the [[Shendan Ocean|Shendan]] and [[Aethiopian Ocean|Aethiopian]] coasts. Balboa has 23 public airports, of which 6 are designated as international and 17 serve domestic and regional traffic. The country's principal gateway is [[Sant Cristòfor International Airport]] (SCI), which handled approximately 34.8 million passengers in 2025 and serves as the primary hub for the flag carrier [[Aeroístmus]] and the low-cost carrier [[RapidAir (Balboa)|RapidAir]].

The [[Balboa Airports Authority]], a government agency under the [[Ministry of Transport (Balboa)|Ministry of Transport]], owns and operates all public airports in the country. The authority was established in 1973 following the [[Treaty of Areza]] and the transfer of the [[Balboa Canal|canal zone]] to Balboan sovereignty, consolidating previously separate municipal and provincial airport administrations under a single national body.

