== Naming conventions ==

Balboan airport ICAO codes follow the convention of the IATA code followed by the suffix "IB" (for Istme de Balboa). For example, Sant Cristòfor International Airport has IATA code SCI and ICAO code SCIB. The sole exception is the [[International City of Areza]], which is not part of Balboa and whose airport ([[Areza International Airport]]) uses the ICAO prefix AEIB.

Three airports are named after historical figures: [[Cecilio Ríos International Airport]] is named after [[Cecilio Ríos]], the fourth president of the Republic of Balboa (1956–1962), who negotiated the [[Twelve Guarantees]] and signed the [[Treaty of Balboa Harbour]]; [[Amelio Perez Airport]] is named after [[Amelio Perez]], a governor of Estret Province assassinated in 1989; and [[Marie Torres Airport]] is named after [[Marie Torres]], a pioneering Balboan aviator.

